WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Elena owns a participating whole life policy.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.320
Participating means it can share in the insurer's divisible surplus through

3
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.400
policy dividends under its terms.

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.360
A nonparticipating policy does not provide that participation.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.380
Neither label tells us whether the coverage is temporary or permanent.

6
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.080
A declared dividend can reflect the insurer's experience with claims,

7
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.540
investments and expenses. It is not a guaranteed future

8
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.960
amount merely because dividends have been paid before.

9
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.920
Keep the policy's contractual guarantees separate from a current dividend

10
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.060
illustration. Under Maryland's rule, the insurer determines and

11
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.780
apportions the stated surplus annually for participating policies.

12
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.240
That duty does not guarantee a positive dividend every year.

13
00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:57.702
Assume Elena's insurer has declared a four hundred dollar dividend.

14
00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:03.222
Under the cash option, she receives that available dividend as money.

15
00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:08.382
Under premium reduction, the dividend is applied toward the premium due.

16
00:01:08.982 --> 00:01:13.502
If that premium is twelve hundred dollars, applying four hundred leaves

17
00:01:13.502 --> 00:01:15.622
eight hundred dollars to pay from other funds.

18
00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.922
The dividend has not erased every later premium.

19
00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:21.462
It is being used for this payment.

20
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:26.282
Taking cash also does not mean surrendering the entire policy.

21
00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:32.622
Follow the selected transaction carefully: distributing a dividend, paying

22
00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:36.942
a premium and surrendering protection are different actions with different

23
00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:38.482
consequences for the contract.

24
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.300
Elena can instead leave the declared dividend with the insurer to

25
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.500
accumulate interest under the policy's available option.

26
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:51.980
Assume four hundred dollars remains for a full year at a

27
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:56.520
hypothetical three percent simple annual rate, with no additions or

28
00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.190
withdrawals. Twelve dollars of interest brings the total to four hundred

29
00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:06.460
twelve dollars. The interest-crediting terms and access rights come from

30
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.900
the actual arrangement. The declared dividend and the interest earned

31
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.040
afterward are separate items.

32
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.600
Interest on accumulated dividends generally creates taxable interest income,

33
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.440
covered more fully in the tax lessons.

34
00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.300
Do not label the accumulation balance an extra death benefit purchased

35
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.162
with insurance. Under an available one-year term dividend option, the

36
00:02:31.162 --> 00:02:35.442
dividend buys additional temporary protection for the specified year under

37
00:02:35.442 --> 00:02:40.462
the contract's conditions. A paid-up-additions option instead

38
00:02:40.462 --> 00:02:44.822
buys an additional amount of permanent insurance that requires no more

39
00:02:44.822 --> 00:02:46.842
premiums for that purchased addition.

40
00:02:47.602 --> 00:02:52.142
Suppose a stated offer uses Elena's four hundred dollar dividend to

41
00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:55.662
buy two thousand dollars of paid-up additional whole life.

42
00:02:55.662 --> 00:02:59.562
The two thousand is added insurance, not a four hundred dollar

43
00:02:59.562 --> 00:03:03.402
cash account and not proof that her entire base policy is

44
00:03:03.402 --> 00:03:07.222
paid up. The amount a dividend buys depends on the applicable

45
00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:12.282
purchase basis. Check availability, eligibility and the actual

46
00:03:12.282 --> 00:03:17.580
quotation. Another outline concept is using dividends

47
00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.100
toward paid-up insurance or shortening the premium-paying period.

48
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.540
Under an available arrangement, accumulated dividend values can help fund the

49
00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.380
amount needed to make the existing policy paid up sooner.

50
00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.100
That goal is different from buying a small paid-up addition each

51
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:39.640
year. It is also different from choosing reduced paid-up nonforfeiture and

52
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.660
accepting a smaller base benefit.

53
00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:47.360
Most importantly, a projection that future dividends will cover premiums is

54
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.180
not confirmation that the policy is already paid up.

55
00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:55.180
If dividends fall, an owner relying on premium offset may need

56
00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.860
to resume payments from other money.

57
00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.900
Confirm actual contractual status with the insurer.

58
00:04:00.594 --> 00:04:04.374
Maryland's participating-policy provision includes the stated cash,

59
00:04:05.074 --> 00:04:09.774
premium-payment, paid-up-addition and interest-accumulation choices, with a

60
00:04:09.774 --> 00:04:11.954
term-policy exception for the latter two.

61
00:04:12.894 --> 00:04:14.914
An insurer may offer additional choices.

62
00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:19.654
This does not make every textbook option mandatory on every policy.

63
00:04:20.754 --> 00:04:24.394
An ordinary participating policy must specify what happens if a different

64
00:04:24.394 --> 00:04:28.564
option is not elected within the stated thirty-day period after the

65
00:04:28.564 --> 00:04:33.124
dividend becomes payable. Elena therefore checks the actual option and

66
00:04:33.124 --> 00:04:38.264
deadline before deciding. On an exam, first identify whether

67
00:04:38.264 --> 00:04:43.324
the question asks about receiving cash, reducing a premium, earning interest,

68
00:04:43.964 --> 00:04:48.064
adding temporary coverage, adding permanent coverage or making the existing

69
00:04:48.064 --> 00:04:49.304
insurance paid up.
